Now CSS. Add auction styles after sold styles or before page screens. Need ensure `.auction-overlay` etc. Let's write robust CSS. Need consider viewport safe areas and small screens. Use existing variables.

Let's craft CSS around line 1220 before `/* PAGE SCREENS */`. Add:
```
/* AUCTION */
.auction-overlay { position:absolute; inset:0; z-index:75; background: radial-gradient(...); display:flex; flex-direction:column; animation:fadeIn .35s ease both; }
.auction-overlay[hidden] { display:none; }
.auction-room { flex:1; min-height:0; display:flex; flex-direction:column; position:relative; overflow:hidden; }
.auction-head ...
...
```
Need use `--font-display`. Fine.

Details:
- `.auction-stage` flex 1, min-height 0, position relative.
- `.auction-beam` use `clip-path: polygon(42% 0, 58% 0, 100% 100%, 0 100%)` maybe. Background gradient. `filter: blur(8px)`.
- Add floor via `.auction-stage::before` radial gradient at bottom.
- `.auction-stage::after` vignette.
- Crowd z-index 4, podium z-index 6, bid panel 8, sold stamp 9.
- Bidders positioned. Need ensure front bidders not covered by podium: podium z-index 6, bidders 4, so podium covers them if overlap. But front bidders flank. Fine. Signs z-index within bidder; bidder z-index 4, sign appears above but still under podium if overlapping. They are at sides, okay.
- Add `.bidder-back-left` etc.
- For bidder `animation: bidderSway ...`; if we set `animation-delay` individually, okay.
- `.bidder.is-bidding` maybe z-index 7 so sign appears above podium? If sign near podium, could raise above. Add `.bidder.is-bidding { z-index:7; }` but crowd is parent z-index 4; child z-index can't escape stacking context if parent has z-index. If `.auction-crowd` has z-index 4, all bidders under podium. Could set `.auction-crowd` z-index 7 and podium z-index 6? Then bidders could appear in front of podium, not desired. Or no z-index on crowd, each bidder has z-index; but `.auction-crowd` position absolute and no z-index, children can stack relative to stage. Let's set `.auction-crowd { position:absolute; inset:0; pointer-events:none; }` no z-index; bidders `z-index:4`; podium `z-index:6`; bid panel 8. If bidder sign overlaps podium, it's under. But front/mid sides don't overlap much. Fine. Back bidders signs near top, no overlap.
- `.auction-podium` maybe z-index 6.
- `.auction-sold-stamp` z-index 9.
- `.auction-bid-panel.is-bump strong { animation: bidBump .28s ... }` We'll toggle class in JS; animation only runs when class added. Need remove/re-add each time; can use `void el.offsetWidth`.
- `.auction-sold-stamp` hidden attribute works; but when hidden then show, class add next frame.
- `.auction-continue` style. `.primary-btn` has height 56 maybe; set height 44 and width 156. Need inspect primary-btn CSS; likely okay. Use flex.
- Footer safe bottom.

Responsive: On short screens (max-height 700), reduce podium image and stage? Add media query:
```
@media (max-height: 720px) {
  .auction-head { flex-basis:50px; }
  #auctionImg { width:138px; height:138px; }
  .auction-podium { bottom:8%; }
  .auction-foot { flex-basis:78px; }
  .bidder { width:48px; height:94px; }
}
```
But child sizes use px; can use transform scale? Not necessary. We can add a simple media query. Existing app has mobile height 844. Fine.

Need ensure `#auctionImg` width and height set. `img { max-width:100% }`; okay.

Let's write CSS.

